# MAGT: Mask-Aware Generative Transformer for Image Inpainting

![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-blue.svg)

This repository contains the official PyTorch implementation of our paper:

**"Advancements in Image Inpainting: A Deep Learning and GAN-Based Perspective with Defined Research Objectives"**

---

## 🔍 Overview
This project introduces a novel image inpainting framework based on a Mask-Aware Generative Transformer (MAGT). The model integrates:

- Dual-branch attention modules (semantic + texture attention)
- Structure prediction module (edge-aware)
- Multi-scale discriminator (GAN-based)

The method demonstrates state-of-the-art performance on CelebA-HQ, ADE20K, and Paris StreetView datasets under irregular masking conditions.

---

## 📁 Dataset
We use three public datasets:

- [CelebA-HQ](https://mmlab.ie.cuhk.edu.hk/projects/CelebA.html)
- [Paris StreetView](https://graphics.cs.cmu.edu/projects/inpaintPS/)
- [ADE20K](https://groups.csail.mit.edu/vision/datasets/ADE20K/)

### 💡 Mask Generation
Irregular masks are generated using the method from Liu et al., 2018 (free-form brush stroke simulation). Scripts included in `/masks/`.

---

## 🧠 Model Architecture
```
Input Image + Binary Mask
        │
        ▼
   Coarse Generator
        │
        ▼
Refinement Generator with:
 - Mask-Aware Attention
 - Edge Guidance
        │
        ▼
     Decoder
        │
        ▼
Completed Image
```
See `/models/` for architecture definitions.

